Objective:

The objective of this project is to create a Recipe Manager application using Python. This project will consolidate the fundamental concepts learned throughout the course, including data types, control flow, functions, file handling, and basic data manipulation. The Recipe Manager will allow users to add, view, search, edit, and delete recipes, demonstrating practical application of Python programming skills.

Instructions:

1. Set Up Your Project Structure
Create a Python script named recipe_manager.py.
Organize your project files into appropriate directories (e.g., data for storing recipe data files).
2. Define Recipe Data Structure
Decide on the structure of a recipe (e.g., title, ingredients, instructions).
Implement a data structure to represent a recipe (e.g., dictionary, class).
3. Implement Core Functionalities
Create functions to:
Add a new recipe
View all recipes
Search for recipes by title or ingredients
Edit a recipe
Delete a recipe
4. File Handling
Implement functions to save and load recipes from a file using text or JSON format.
Ensure the data persists between program runs.
5. User Interface
Design a simple command-line interface (CLI) for interacting with the Recipe Manager.
Clearly display options and guide the user through the available functionalities.
6. Testing and Validation
Test each functionality thoroughly to ensure it works as expected.
Handle edge cases gracefully (e.g., invalid user inputs).
Validate user inputs to prevent errors and ensure data integrity.
7. Documentation and Comments
Document your code using clear and concise comments.
Provide a brief overview of the project and how to use the Recipe Manager.
8. Bonus Features (Optional)
Implement additional features such as categorizing recipes, adding ratings, or supporting multiple users.
Improve the user interface with colors or ASCII art.
9. Project Presentation
Prepare a brief presentation demonstrating your Recipe Manager.
Showcase the functionalities and explain how they were implemented.
Discuss any challenges faced during the development process and how you overcame them.
10. Submission
Submit your project files along with any necessary documentation.
Include instructions on how to run the Recipe Manager.
11. Additional Tips
Break down the project into smaller tasks and tackle them one at a time.
Use version control (e.g., Git) to track changes and collaborate if working in a group.
Don't hesitate to consult Python documentation, online resources, or ask for help when stuck.